---
model: agent:gpt-5.6-sol:medium,agent:opus:medium
effort: high
budget:
  maxTurns: 40
  timeout: 45m
prompt:
  system: >-
    You are running inside a developer's git working tree at {{workDir}}
    on branch {{branch}}, which is open as pull request #{{number}}{{#if title}} ({{title}}){{/if}}.
    Read the `gavel pr status` snapshot the user pastes, identify the failing
    GitHub Actions jobs and unresolved review comments, and edit files in place
    to fix them. Prefer minimal, targeted edits over rewrites.
    Do not run any commit-related commands and do not push: each turn's changes
    are committed and pushed for you, after which the PR status is re-polled and
    any remaining failures are fed back to you.
workflow:
  verify:
    maxIterations: 3
    scope: changed
    # --follow is required: the status rollup exits 0 while checks are still
    # in progress, so polling without it green-lights the run before CI has
    # re-run the freshly pushed commit. --fail-fast keeps the loop honest but
    # cheap: it returns at the first definitive failure instead of holding the
    # turn open for every slow scan. That matters because this command declares
    # no timeout of its own, so it is bounded by captain's 10-minute
    # DefaultCmdTimeout — and a CodeQL analysis alone can run for seven.
    #
    # No --actions here on purpose: the agent needs the full red picture, and
    # scoping the gate would let a check outside the selector stay broken while
    # the loop reports green.
    commands:
      - gavel pr status --follow --fail-fast --logs --tail-logs 40
  commits:
    # A real commit per turn, not the `on: turn` default of fixup: the chain is
    # squashed only at end of run, and these commits are pushed as they are cut.
    - on: turn
      mode: commit
      gates: cheap
---
Fix the failures and unresolved comments visible in this PR status snapshot:

```
{{statusText}}
```
{{#if url}}
The pull request URL is {{url}}.
{{/if}}
{{#if unresolvedComments}}
There are {{unresolvedComments}} unresolved review comments; address each one.
{{/if}}
